{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1ca17220c02cf118c478f77e87464e44a03671b15f270792a0d3810537f52b85","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"supabitapp/supacode@81cba5538f1e snapshot 66b194affe240b6a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1c32d638bc850b053ec4433c0696121fc397d08857021e4354f72df2bc4a185a"],"source_ids":["src_464ab6303eae54498ea24394368c4b63"],"text":"A `supacode` CLI manages worktrees, tabs, splits, and repos; sessions export repo, worktree, tab, and surface IDs, and `supacode://` deeplinks mirror CLI actions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3e6ade29cc1fa6f941efcaaa365948cd4e3ecf6f380355301efb2c4541a9d5a4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"supabitapp/supacode@81cba5538f1e snapshot 66b194affe240b6a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_129080a4b6e9ed8870c7b20efc9fa9786ae98d43d73c07834cc5f088b9b07f8b"],"source_ids":["src_464ab6303eae54498ea24394368c4b63"],"text":"Plain folders are first-class alongside git repos, getting a persistent terminal with tabs, scripts, and pinning but without git-only tools; remote URLs can be cloned into a folder.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_48b385d754319bff29becc4179c6723523812ddeb10ed4b5e8e1cff98cdc9a75","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"supabitapp/supacode@81cba5538f1e snapshot 66b194affe240b6a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3342e9b6cae668780004853c546f1f1a458d492a8c1252d4b427b1d368d773d3","slc_d1e2283b217a625986858acb3a44d048fda931d2c033c858a2de61b4f4fa8656"],"source_ids":["src_464ab6303eae54498ea24394368c4b63"],"text":"Supacode is a native macOS application (macOS 26.0+ required) that acts as a command center for running coding agents in parallel.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6e34f8bfa3b5989771a5febc10c07025fa8b4c72ae26bc09f9adc23b33bd62fc","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"supabitapp/supacode@81cba5538f1e snapshot 66b194affe240b6a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a596bbc279933987d72e144c5ae32d059936264c59dc43bc093bc03407e7fa60"],"source_ids":["src_464ab6303eae54498ea24394368c4b63"],"text":"Sessions run inside zmx, a session daemon, rather than as app children, so quitting and relaunching reattaches sessions with scrollback; this is on by default with an optional teardown quit.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_758b40717cbc9dcbcf1720de55c49469e07c1d43675592a097640d4ebaa68915","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"supabitapp/supacode@81cba5538f1e snapshot 66b194affe240b6a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_12a305fba8d4de3eb4d1292f23dd90ec2c3a5e82fb6bfca915b3cf72102f659c","slc_16d422d87c4acc51cd28c30cbc241f3a2c2f3e434b9bb167eab6266b781198e9","slc_3e72cb1bd80bb368cfe2bcd57cc5acfd28cd29e30a983b11bd0fb25ff807ada3","slc_d1e2283b217a625986858acb3a44d048fda931d2c033c858a2de61b4f4fa8656"],"source_ids":["src_464ab6303eae54498ea24394368c4b63"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors use mise for a pinned toolchain, git submodules, and make targets (doctor, build-ghostty-xcframework, build-app, run-app); on macOS 26.4+ Xcode 26.3 is needed because the pinned Zig 0.15.2 linker cannot link that SDK.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7c2c27d715b8bd31b8112f00542baa3a50f5307df3d4aab7ed85cd430168ac74","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"supabitapp/supacode@81cba5538f1e snapshot 66b194affe240b6a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3e30cf437c538a5ad9cc8099eb75d285988ab9d5acb69bd4cf61adf024f7747e","slc_bdb9bd6d4d5523a4279a0c14c6b098a8d9ca9e8b0cdd283885deda7857ebb96e"],"source_ids":["src_464ab6303eae54498ea24394368c4b63","src_d53e5dccfbbd5a82802a212999f37b3f"],"text":"Key dependencies include The Composable Architecture for app state, GhosttyKit as the terminal emulator, Sparkle for updates, PostHog for analytics, and Sentry for error tracking.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d5a7b591406a7b56b73604c4bc37ab25a0676b514e26b453f693b7a76dc094aa","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"supabitapp/supacode@81cba5538f1e snapshot 66b194affe240b6a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_99e27c4aa6d4cc85932376e1f6d8131b4450d1e3465466c31f9adfa5557256ff"],"source_ids":["src_464ab6303eae54498ea24394368c4b63"],"text":"The app detects the coding agent per pane (busy, awaiting input, idle) via installed hooks, supporting Claude, Codex, and Copilot locally and over SSH, and drives notifications.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e9f9f2cc74f20d628e884dc302b8f6db8d319e9f5ce0e1d0789172f7f56c5286","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"supabitapp/supacode@81cba5538f1e snapshot 66b194affe240b6a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_089567cdaede062e95219583f9a7875be8e86b734461eb9b39390f013f1dd3e9"],"source_ids":["src_464ab6303eae54498ea24394368c4b63"],"text":"With GitHub integration enabled, each worktree's PR state, checks, and merge readiness display in the sidebar and refresh live with a configurable merge strategy.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_efcc6ae171408e9bb261b1a8236a8fc211f10be1aa829a8eff985b5f2f538449","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"supabitapp/supacode@81cba5538f1e snapshot 66b194affe240b6a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c223811e5a634567dc2180a3f7541b0a86751bb1d4474286c836b929deebcabe"],"source_ids":["src_464ab6303eae54498ea24394368c4b63"],"text":"Remote SSH repositories are supported in beta: git probes and terminals share one multiplexed SSH connection, and with zmx on the host, remote sessions survive dropped connections and sleep.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_efd1bb32ede8674e3d21bf6832a8092f258a99af4fdaab2dd71da7d9c011ad88","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"supabitapp/supacode@81cba5538f1e snapshot 66b194affe240b6a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b3d07674ebc9c186dec7ba6cdceb37aeb85a75a9abca4338def48be39ce5eb4f","slc_f56dca3cefa2695d60c536f10d63c9f7dfa840af2f8a7b50bc1ab05bbb65d840"],"source_ids":["src_464ab6303eae54498ea24394368c4b63"],"text":"Each task gets its own git worktree and real terminal so agents run in parallel without colliding; worktrees can be created from the sidebar, hotkey, command palette, CLI, or deeplink.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f6e32765a27d77f4a7b859e4b7fa018a79ab2107199e41f1cbff84b6f7a47b33","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"supabitapp/supacode@81cba5538f1e snapshot 66b194affe240b6a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0f77aaad71f732504a026d355947da064aed77ae5becab9bfbdb5ac6eefa5c55","slc_6bfba5f83a02b6b6a0961e23fdad9269c29445284e9f99540d174cb0499fbd88","slc_81baa837ce7aa51e645b1450d851b683861eeb614d4bfa11fafccc2e9dab6fa9","slc_dbb2aacef72790e3a358ab1052b3320d2fda9e8f46dbb5964120f65ffe11dc5f"],"source_ids":["src_464ab6303eae54498ea24394368c4b63","src_d53e5dccfbbd5a82802a212999f37b3f"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributions require opening an issue first, waiting for a `ready` label, then a focused linked PR; a human, never an AI agent, must be the accountable author, and code follows Swift 6/TCA style rules checked by `make check`.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_fbd2c36d4c3662bb20f026d01467ae112b5cb0ef9fae0dfe63eb0e6a792f7104","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"supabitapp/supacode@81cba5538f1e snapshot 66b194affe240b6a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_089567cdaede062e95219583f9a7875be8e86b734461eb9b39390f013f1dd3e9","slc_3e30cf437c538a5ad9cc8099eb75d285988ab9d5acb69bd4cf61adf024f7747e"],"source_ids":["src_464ab6303eae54498ea24394368c4b63"],"text":"Terminal rendering uses libghostty with tabs, splits, per-surface backgrounds, and theme sync; auto-updates come through Sparkle with a selectable channel.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:15:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c9d11a9b992e4ee0bd2de32d87b3cbdc"}
